      "data": {
        "title": "Declarations Supply Default Handles; Ports May Override Them",
        "statement": "A node Declaration may reference one graph-backed Handle definition as its default handle presentation. Every Port node exposes a structural handle port that may reference another Handle definition, overriding the Declaration default for that endpoint.",
        "status": "framed",
        "confidence": "plausible",
        "notes": "Handle resolution is Port override, then Declaration default, then system fallback. Handle definitions own representation only. Ports continue to own endpoint identity, capability, direction, data type, allowed edges, and behavior. Collectors are derived handles resolved through the same presentation rule.",
        "definitionKey": "idea",
